.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead resource remove" 1  "bead resource remove " 
.SH NAME
bead resource remove \- Remove one or more local resource keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead resource remove\fR [\fB\-\-fencing\-token\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-key\fR> <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove normalized resource declarations from an issue.
.PP
This changes scheduling metadata in the current native workspace only; it
does not coordinate or unlock resources in another store. Removing keys from
an in\-progress issue requires its lease fencing token when applicable.
.PP
EXAMPLE:
  bead resource remove <ID> \-\-key gpu:0
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEYS>\fR
Resource key; repeat for multiple keys
.TP
\fB\-\-fencing\-token\fR \fI<FENCING_TOKEN>\fR
Fencing token for a leased in\-progress issue
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Issue ID
